# Announcements module (P7) — demo requests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
#
# One-time local setup (Development) is the same as users.http.
# Prerequisites: scheduling.http + lifecycle.http (active term, a subject the professor teaches, a registered student).
# Decision ANN: professors only, scoped to a subject (all groups or one group). Only "urgent" notifies students.

@host = http://localhost:5080
@professorToken = paste-the-teaching-professors-token-here
@studentToken = paste-a-registered-students-token-here
@subjectId = paste-a-subject-id-here
@announcementId = paste-the-id-from-the-post-here

### Professor: post an urgent, pinned announcement → 201 (students of the subject get a notification)
POST {{host}}/api/announcements
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectId": "{{subjectId}}",
  "title": "Midterm moved",
  "body": "الامتحان يوم الأحد في القاعة ٣٠٢",
  "priority": "urgent",
  "isPinned": true,
  "expiresAt": null
}

### Student (registered) / professor (teaching) / admin: the subject's announcements — pinned first, then newest
GET {{host}}/api/announcements?subjectId={{subjectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Student: the feed across every registered subject (expired ones hidden)
GET {{host}}/api/announcements/feed
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Author / teacher: edit
PUT {{host}}/api/announcements/{{announcementId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "subjectId": "{{subjectId}}", "title": "Midterm moved to Monday", "body": "Hall 302, 10:00", "priority": "high", "isPinned": false }

### Author / teacher: soft delete → 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/announcements/{{announcementId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
